fine-print bundled fonts
========================

These fonts are third-party font software, bundled UNMODIFIED (no
subsetting, renaming or re-encoding) so the renderer can draw standard-14
text that a PDF does not embed. fine-print reads them; it never changes or
re-distributes them separately. Each is licensed under the SIL Open Font
License, Version 1.1, whose text is in the file named below for that family.

Approved by the owner on 2026-10-21 (fonts are the one relaxed third-party
category; see the envelope's RULES.md). Chosen by measuring each family's
WinAnsi advance widths against fine-print's standard-14 tables
(src/Writer/Fonts/StandardMetrics.php): Tinos and Cousine match exactly;
Arimo, the Croscore sans, differs on one glyph (florin, 279 against 556), so
the sans is Liberation Sans, which matches.

